<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Czechs</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Czechs are a West Slavic people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, in the present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a>. Within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>, Czechs pressed for autonomy comparable to that given to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> in 1867, leading to persistent political conflict, especially in Bohemia. Czech nationalism contributed to the empire's dissolution and the creation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> in 1918.</p></div>
